							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 50<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=339"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13929#msg13929"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13929#msg13929">Re: New Bitch Topic from Top Ten List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #22 on:</b> January 25, 2005, 04:07:09 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Um....that&#039;s pretty much the way the server has been since AoD was in power.  If anyone set the precedence for the &quot;i&#039;ll do it when I want&quot; attitude it was them.   It sucks, believe me I know, but it&#039;s quite satisfying beating them at their own game.<br /><br />This brings up another topic.  I&#039;ve been stupified for years how people think the top guilds are 100% model citizens, and how they can do no wrong.  I should be more specific when I say people I guess, this applies to your average joe on the server.  The high end guilds all pretty much know how things are once theres enough headbutting.   <br /><br />What is it?  Is it just the average joe being impressed by the ESPN Highlights?  Is it the high end players blowing smoke up your ass?  Friend of a friend of a friend of a guild tell you what super people they are?   I just don&#039;t get it.  It&#039;s actually kind of scary how easy it is to throw a spin on a large group of people.
						</td>
					</tr>
