							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13836#msg13836">Quote from: Slayyerr on January 22, 2005, 12:34:54 pm</a></div><div class="quote">IMO its not that Ascent is going backwards, it&#039;s that they are not handling things in a decent matter. They are mostly FoT members and some Forsaken. The old Ascent is gone to other games. Thats why you see Ascent doing the things they do now. Training and jumping back into the Time rotation between Conviction and RoS. They do not care about a rotation or agreement. Averiel and his warp team continue to warp to gear thmemselves. In other words alot of Ascent members now cheat in order to help better themselves. Along with some DA/EiE members &lt;cough&gt; &quot;Fletchera&quot; &quot;Ferrieciean&quot; &quot;Anabesi&quot; Good to know that cheating is now one way for the top guilds to remain there. O and by ignoring a set rotation just because they want to. Flame away, but Ascent is no longer the Asent of Old. They are gimp and struggling to survive and will pretty much take anyone that has an account and close to 70 atm.<br /></div><br />it&#039;s spelled Ferriciean~  and i&#039;m in ascent, not eie/da  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" /><br /><br />i know we&#039;ve already duked this out in tells, but.... my question remains:<br /><br />how do you see people warping, if you&#039;re not cheating?  =)  i mean.. the day you accused me of warping (which, btw, i happend to have run the whole way~.&nbsp; as i explained, bards can &quot;fade&quot; agro)... you were in a totally different part of the zone from where i was.  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm13.gif" alt="cwm13" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
